  "passage": "Riverside School is excited to announce its 40th Anniversary Community Fair this Saturday from 10 am to 4 pm. Despite the unpredictable British weather, all activities will proceed indoors if necessary. The event aims to entertain families and friends with a variety of attractions, including live music, craft stalls, and games. A highlight will be the costume contest, judged by our beloved history teacher, Mr. Jones, who is known for his impressive moustache. Students are encouraged to come with their classmates and enjoy the day. To manage crowds, we've introduced a new ticketing system at the entrance. For food lovers, try our special Irish coffee—be aware that its bitter taste might not suit everyone. Also, visit our café for refreshments served in charming saucers. Don't miss this opportunity to celebrate our school's history and community spirit!",
